@startuml render-pipeline-sequence
'==============================================================================
' Render pipeline — end-to-end: wizard to mp4
'
' MIRRORS: docs/RENDER_PIPELINE.md §1 "The happy path"
'   (the ```mermaid block in that section is CANONICAL — edit both or neither)
'
' Rendered by:  plantuml docs/diagrams/render-pipeline-sequence.puml
' GitHub does NOT render .puml. This file exists for export to PNG/SVG.
'==============================================================================

title Render pipeline — end-to-end: wizard to mp4

autonumber

actor User
participant WIZ as CreationWizard\n(browser)
participant API as POST /api/workflows/generate\n(Next.js)
participant DB as Supabase\nrender_jobs
participant W as render-worker\n(node --import tsx)
participant TTS as TTS cascade
participant MED as Media sources
participant FF as ffmpeg + ffprobe

== Queue boundary ==

User -> WIZ: completes 5 steps, clicks "Send to Queue"
WIZ -> API: POST { workflow, script, subject, aspectRatio,\nvoice*, music*, subtitle*, tone, beats[] }

note right of API
  beats[] is the whole point — one beat per
  scene, each with the asset the user picked.
  The user's pick is ordered FIRST in urls[],
  so the worker reads it as urls[0].
end note

API -> API: validate script; normalise beats[]\n(drop empty-text beats, default duration 3)
API -> DB: INSERT render_jobs\norchestration_state='queued', logs={...beats, settings}
API --> WIZ: 200 { success, jobId, beatCount }
WIZ --> User: router.push(/dashboard?job=<jobId>)

note right of DB
  orchestration_state is TEXT and is matched
  by claim_render_job against a literal
  allow-list. It is a STATE MACHINE, not a
  settings bag — all config goes in logs.
end note

== Claim ==

loop poll (every few seconds)
  W -> DB: claim_render_job(worker_id, lease_token, lease_ms=900000)
  DB --> W: 1 row, or empty set
end

DB --> W: job row (state 'claimed', attempt_count+1)

note over W, DB
  Claimable when state IN ('queued','retryable')
  OR state IN ('claimed','rendering','publishing')
     AND lease_expires_at < now()
  AND attempt_count < max_attempts (default 3)
  ORDER BY created_at ASC FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
end note

note right of W
  params = { ...columns, ...JSON.parse(job.logs) }
  Beats and every setting come from logs, because
  the worker's JSON.parse(job.orchestration_state)
  throws on a plain state string and yields {}.
end note

== Per-beat render loop ==

loop for each beat
  W -> TTS: synthesize(text, provider, voice)
  TTS --> W: audio url + duration

  note over TTS
    cascade: elevenlabs -> omniroute -> keyless
    keyless sub-cascade: Edge TTS
      -> Google Translate TTS -> synthetic WAV
    TTS failure does NOT fail the beat:
    the clip gets a silent anullsrc track.
  end note

  W -> MED: resolve beat media, then download
  MED --> W: local media file

  note right of MED
    chain: selectedVideo.url || imageUrl
      || videoUrl || clipUrl || urls[0]
    fallbacks: OmniRoute images (empty body!)
      -> Pollinations  <- de-facto source
  end note

  W -> FF: isVideoFile() — still vs video from BYTES
  W -> FF: ffprobe audio duration (exact frame math)
  W -> FF: encode clip_i.mp4\n(loop+zoompan if still, -t if video,\nlibx264 + aac, subtitles via drawtext)
end

== Concat, music, completion ==

W -> FF: concat -f concat -safe 0 -c copy -> concat_temp.mp4

opt musicVolume > 0 AND pixabay key
  W -> MED: GET pixabay.com/api/audio/?key=...&q=...
  MED --> W: track.preview
  W -> FF: sidechaincompress ducking + amix -> final mp4
  note right of FF
    [bgm][main1]sidechaincompress=threshold=0.08:ratio=4\n  :attack=5:release=50[bgm_ducked]
    [main2][bgm_ducked]amix=inputs=2:duration=first[aout]
    A BGM failure is caught and the render
    continues without music — it never fails the job.
  end note
end

W -> DB: complete_render_job(job, worker, lease_token, output_url, logs)
DB --> W: true — only if the lease is still valid

note right of DB
  requires ALL of: id, worker_id, lease_token,
  AND lease_expires_at > now()
  writes: orchestration_state='completed',
          status='completed', output_url
  output file: public/renders/<jobId>.mp4
end note

== Failure ==

alt any step throws
  W -> DB: fail_render_job(job, worker, lease_token, error)
  note right of DB
    'retryable' while attempt_count < max_attempts,
    else 'failed'. attempt_count is incremented
    at CLAIM time, so max_attempts=3 = 3 total tries.
  end note
end

@enduml
